// spec: a qualifier naming a specialization whose partial specializations both match and neither is more specialized is ambiguous wherever it is written, a compile error as C++ has it ([temp.spec.partial.match] 1; clang: "ambiguous partial specializations"): the callee of a call `S<const int, int*>::v()`, a nested qualifier `S<...>::Inner::w()`, a member function's address `&S<...>::v`, a type through one `S<...>::Inner x;`, and a call in a function template's instance
// error: ambiguous_partial_specializations_in_an_expression_are_error.kpp:11: error: the partial specializations of S<const int32, int32*> are ambiguous: S<const T, U>
